                        "entry_id": "b6c91e8e-1f8d-30b5-8fa2-ea67bf91da04",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A tiny biting insect found in South America."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f70f314a-fea4-4f0c-b8a9-5c770e610daf",
                                "sense_id": "7c0ece52-da21-3311-b62f-d4030410c87c",
                                "text": "Mosquitoes and polverines, little midges so small as to be scarcely visible, rose in a cloud from the water and settled on our hands and faces."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "eeead584-5d7c-46f3-b794-bcd343c1124f",
                                "sense_id": "7c0ece52-da21-3311-b62f-d4030410c87c",
                                "text": "The polverines, however, were so small and numerous that even though we massacred fifty with a slap it seemed to make no difference to the hazy black cloud which hung around our heads."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "335e957a-3be3-4a29-bde9-a626654065ab",
                                "sense_id": "7c0ece52-da21-3311-b62f-d4030410c87c",
                                "text": "But all were more tolerable than those polverines."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
